WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:03.135
-Two centrist Democrats

00:00:03.135 --> 00:00:05.138
are holding
Joe Biden's agenda hostage,

00:00:05.138 --> 00:00:07.506
while Republicans threaten
to crater the economy

00:00:07.506 --> 00:00:09.008
as a negotiating tactic.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:11.310
Oh, and also, we found out
that the previous president

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:13.213
called a White House aide
from Air Force One

00:00:13.213 --> 00:00:14.947
to defend the size of his penis.

00:00:14.947 --> 00:00:17.550
And I know one of those stories
is bigger than the other,

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:19.285
but we can do both.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:21.120
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.891
♪♪

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:28.060
No, I just meant that one
of the stories

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.729
is bigger than the other.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:33.032
Yeah, it had nothing to do
with the size of your, you know.

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.567
No, I --

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:37.270
I didn't know a lot of people
have been saying that, no.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:38.371
Okay.

00:00:39.773 --> 00:00:42.141
Okay.

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:44.410
Alright.

00:00:44.410 --> 00:00:46.112
Love to Melania.

00:00:46.112 --> 00:00:48.214
[ Laughter ]
Sorry about that. I just

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:50.482
think he has a lot
of free time right now.

00:00:50.482 --> 00:00:51.684
Anyway, back to Congress.

00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:53.319
We're living in a time
of asymmetric

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:54.520
partisan fighting in politics.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:55.955
We have two sides,

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.556
one of which cares
about competent governance;

00:00:57.556 --> 00:00:58.825
and the other, which is willing

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:00.359
to burn everything down
to gain power.

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:01.594
I mean, just look
at the difference

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:03.195
in styles
between Biden and Trump.

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:06.766
Biden with literally cut himself
off during primary debates,

00:01:06.766 --> 00:01:08.234
if his answers went on too long;

00:01:08.234 --> 00:01:10.135
and Trump will spend an hour
at a rally

00:01:10.135 --> 00:01:12.905
meandering aimlessly
about Bobby Knight or Pavarotti

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:16.042
or some other B-list celebrity
he met one time at the 21 Club.

00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:17.644
[ As Trump ]
Luciano Pavarotti --

00:01:17.644 --> 00:01:18.878
oh, he could sing.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.779
He could sing and he loved food.
Loved to eat.

00:01:20.779 --> 00:01:24.517
One time I saw him eat
two entrees and a centerpiece.

00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:27.686
[ Laughter ]
Anyway,

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:29.488
Make America Great Again.

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:32.525
Bernie Sanders
and the Progressive Caucus

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:35.461
in the House are, as we speak,
standing firm in their fight

00:01:35.461 --> 00:01:38.130
to advance a transformative
$3.5 trillion bill

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:40.132
that would invest in everything
from education

00:01:40.132 --> 00:01:41.634
to housing, to healthcare,

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:44.070
a set of priorities they
promised voters they would pass.

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:45.104
Meanwhile, Senate Republicans

00:01:45.104 --> 00:01:46.572
are refusing
to raise the debt limit,

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:49.575
which could lead to a default
and economic catastrophe.

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:51.978
I just wish there was someone
more insightful than me

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:54.246
who could express
the frustrating asymmetry

00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:56.515
between the two parties --
perhaps a newspaper columnist

00:01:56.515 --> 00:01:59.185
or a political consultant,
or someone from a think tank?

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.820 line:0%
-We are so pleased to welcome

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:02.221 line:0%
my friend Steve Van Zandt now,

00:02:02.221 --> 00:02:05.457 line:0%
author of this new memoir,
which, again, is called

00:02:05.457 --> 00:02:07.693 line:0%
"Unrequited Infatuations."

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:10.362 line:0%
-I got to admit it's a little
depressing, at the moment,

00:02:10.362 --> 00:02:11.697 line:0%
a little frustrating.

00:02:11.697 --> 00:02:14.200 line:0%
I just got
this terrible feeling,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.435 line:0%
you know, and I've had this
for a long, long time,

00:02:16.435 --> 00:02:20.306 line:0%
that we are in a war and only
one side is fighting it.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:22.741 line:0%
And I've been feeling that
for decades

00:02:22.741 --> 00:02:28.314 line:0%
and it's really coming
to a very serious place, now,

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:30.817 line:0%
where we might lose
our democracy because of it.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:33.286 line:0%
You know, the two, you know,

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:36.222 line:0%
the Benedict Arnold twins,
they're not helping matters

00:02:36.222 --> 00:02:38.991 line:0%
and they're,
you know, they better --

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:41.027 line:0%
I hope they come around.
I don't know.

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:43.930 line:0%
I don't want to see Manchin
on TV ever again.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.698 line:0%
[ Laughing ]
I mean, I'm sick of his face.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.700
-Oh, man, Joe Manchin,
you better watch out.

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.401
If Little Steven says he's sick
of your face,

00:02:49.401 --> 00:02:51.204
your house boat might end up
burning down

00:02:51.204 --> 00:02:53.239
like Artie Bucco's restaurant.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.141
So happy that this is
where we're at

00:02:55.141 --> 00:02:56.475
with political commentary
right now.

00:02:56.475 --> 00:02:57.910
I'm sick of the well-paid
consultants

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.378
and think tank pundits,

00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:01.180
who clearly know nothing
about actual voters,

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:03.782
shilling for big corporations
and elite institutions.

00:03:03.782 --> 00:03:07.152
Let's get Steve Van Zandt
a show on MSNBC.

00:03:07.152 --> 00:03:08.721
Anybody who spent 45 years

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.189
on a tour bus
with Bruce Springsteen

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:12.324
is definitely used to talking
about politics.

00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:14.026
[ As Steven ]
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
the factory's closed up.

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:15.561
I know. Yep. Yep.

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:17.163
Hard for veterans to find jobs.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:20.499
Bruce, I'd love to get
some sleep before Portland.

00:03:20.499 --> 00:03:22.935
[ Laughter ]
You could call the show...

00:03:22.935 --> 00:03:24.870
...and he can do all his
interviews with politicians,

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:26.706 line:0%
sharing a mic,
"Glory Days"-style.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.974 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.974 --> 00:03:31.377
Very nice work from the graphics
department right there.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.112
[ Laughter ]
And the thing is, he's right.

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:34.580
We're living in an era
of asymmetry

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.548
and Democrats need to start
taking that seriously.

00:03:36.548 --> 00:03:37.950
Republicans ran
through a massive

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:40.786
and unpopular tax cut for the
wealthy and corporations

00:03:40.786 --> 00:03:42.722
without virtually
any public debate.

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.657
Now, they're using the prospect
of a default on our debt,

00:03:45.657 --> 00:03:48.428
which would crater our economy,
as a negotiating tactic,

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:51.163
something Democrats
have never done

00:03:51.163 --> 00:03:52.731
when the shoe has been
on the other foot,

00:03:52.731 --> 00:03:55.101
and, instead of just
abolishing the filibuster,

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:57.136
Democrats are scrambling
because centrists,

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.271
like Manchin and Kyrsten Sinema,

00:03:59.271 --> 00:04:00.573
are making things
more difficult.

00:04:00.573 --> 00:04:01.674
And you better believe,

00:04:01.674 --> 00:04:03.141
every time Democrats fight
with each other,

00:04:03.141 --> 00:04:04.310
Mitch McConnell laughs

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.211
like a haunted doll
in a horror movie.

00:04:06.211 --> 00:04:07.880
Where did little Mitch go?

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:10.750
I -- I left him over there
on that chair.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:11.918
[ As McConnell ]
Uh, I'm right here.

00:04:11.918 --> 00:04:13.786
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.786 --> 00:04:15.254
You left the knives out.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:17.557
[ Halting laugh ]

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:20.826
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.826 --> 00:04:22.862 line:0%
That's why we need
Little Steven in D.C.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.663
[ As Steven ]
Hey, I hear you got a problem

00:04:24.663 --> 00:04:26.265
with a freakin' haunted doll
or some [bleep]

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:27.800
Maybe it needs a whack it
upside the head.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.735
[ Laughter ]

00:04:29.735 --> 00:04:31.771
That's my impression of him
from "Lilyhammer."

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:34.006
[ Laughter ]

00:04:34.006 --> 00:04:35.808 line:0%
I mean,
you've got two senators --

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:37.609 line:0%
Joe Manchin,
who's been called a kingmaker

00:04:37.609 --> 00:04:38.944 line:0%
by fossil fuel executives

00:04:38.944 --> 00:04:40.846 line:0%
and personally profits
from the coal industry;

00:04:40.846 --> 00:04:42.481 line:0%
and Kyrsten Sinema,
who's raked in

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:45.217 line:0%
hundreds of thousands
in donations from Big Pharma

00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:47.052 line:0%
and has been raising money
from business groups --

00:04:47.052 --> 00:04:49.655 line:0%
holding up a bill that would
tackle climate change,

00:04:49.655 --> 00:04:51.124 line:0%
establish paid family leave,

00:04:51.124 --> 00:04:52.858 line:0%
make community college
tuition free,

00:04:52.858 --> 00:04:56.161 line:0%
transform child care,
and expand access to healthcare,

00:04:56.161 --> 00:04:57.330 line:0%
among many other things.

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:59.464 line:0%
Name one thing in this bill

00:04:59.464 --> 00:05:00.633
you think is unpopular --

00:05:00.633 --> 00:05:01.967
paid family leave,

00:05:01.967 --> 00:05:04.403
child care tax credit,
dental benefits for Medicare.

00:05:04.403 --> 00:05:07.806
You think people like
shelling out for dental care?

00:05:07.806 --> 00:05:10.410
So, on top of spending an hour
strapped to a chair,

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.878
watching old episodes of "Maury"

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:13.545
on a TV suspended
from the ceiling

00:05:13.545 --> 00:05:16.515
while a hygienist peels back
your gums with an ice pick,

00:05:16.515 --> 00:05:18.884
floss shaming you
in a Russian accent,

00:05:18.884 --> 00:05:21.521
you have to beg your insurance
company to cover it.

00:05:21.521 --> 00:05:23.423
One time, I got so annoyed
with my dental insurance,

00:05:23.423 --> 00:05:25.491
I said, [bleep] it,
and let all my teeth rot.

00:05:25.491 --> 00:05:26.759
These are just dentures.

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:29.028
When I'm not on the air,
I look like this.

00:05:29.028 --> 00:05:30.296
Okay, guys!

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:32.965
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.965 --> 00:05:34.266
I thought it was going
to be different.

00:05:34.266 --> 00:05:37.169
Guys, you got to show me
the graphics before the show.

00:05:37.169 --> 00:05:39.504
[ Laughter ]
Is there another version
we can use,

00:05:39.504 --> 00:05:41.274
that's not as jarring?

00:05:41.274 --> 00:05:43.910
[ As Giuliani ]
Don't you ever give me
Rudy teeth!

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:47.513
[ Laughter ]

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:50.349
And there's so much emphasis
on the top-line price tag,

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:51.683
as it that matters to anyone.

00:05:51.683 --> 00:05:54.553
First of all, it'll be paid for
by taxing the rich.

00:05:54.553 --> 00:05:56.756
But, more importantly,
instead of complaining

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:59.292
about an abstract number that
doesn't mean anything to anyone,

00:05:59.292 --> 00:06:02.228
why don't you name
one actual thing in this bill

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:03.563
you don't like and would cut?

00:06:03.563 --> 00:06:06.466
Something Manchin and Sinema
have refused to do.

00:06:06.466 --> 00:06:08.567
That's a point Bernie
made recently.

00:06:08.567 --> 00:06:10.803 line:0%
-You ask me about compromise.

00:06:10.803 --> 00:06:12.204 line:0%
I have compromised.

00:06:12.204 --> 00:06:14.673 line:0%
The bill that should've been
passed, in my judgment,

00:06:14.673 --> 00:06:16.341 line:0%
was a $6 trillion bill.

00:06:16.341 --> 00:06:18.911 line:0%
If you take climate change
into consideration,

00:06:18.911 --> 00:06:20.579 line:0%
that's the kind of money
that we need.

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:24.383 line:0%
We've already made
a significant compromise.

00:06:24.383 --> 00:06:28.020 line:0%
-Would you consider a number
less than $3.5 trillion?

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.422 line:0%
-No. Look, we're talking
-Have you talked to Joe Manchin?

00:06:29.422 --> 00:06:31.690 line:0%
-about numbers.
You tell me what we should cut.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.126 line:0%
Tell the working families
of this country

00:06:34.126 --> 00:06:37.864 line:0%
that we don't need to make
child care affordable.

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:40.499 line:0%
Tell the American people
and the younger people

00:06:40.499 --> 00:06:43.236 line:0%
that we should not address
the crisis of climate change

00:06:43.236 --> 00:06:45.004 line:0%
and try to save the planet.

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:46.238 line:0%
Tell the homeless people

00:06:46.238 --> 00:06:48.974 line:0%
that we should not build
affordable housing.

00:06:48.974 --> 00:06:50.543 line:0%
Tell the young people
that we should not make

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:52.644 line:0%
community colleges tuition-free.

00:06:52.644 --> 00:06:54.646
-I like when Bernie
takes on the energy

00:06:54.646 --> 00:06:57.116
of a volunteer at the co-op
when they raise prices.

00:06:57.116 --> 00:06:58.651
[ As Sanders ]
How about you tell people

00:06:58.651 --> 00:07:01.954
that Gala apples are suddenly
$2.99 a pound

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:03.456
[ Laughter ]
and that the Swiss chard

00:07:03.456 --> 00:07:06.058
is now more expensive
than a trip to Disneyland?

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:09.361
Excuse me while I sell my kidney
on the black market,

00:07:09.361 --> 00:07:12.765
so that I can afford to purchase
a tablespoon of quinoa.

00:07:12.765 --> 00:07:14.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:17.302
Now, on one hand, even though
I think he's incredibly wrong

00:07:17.302 --> 00:07:18.970
and self-serving
and destructive,

00:07:18.970 --> 00:07:21.173
you can at least
kind of understand

00:07:21.173 --> 00:07:22.608
where Manchin is coming from.

00:07:22.608 --> 00:07:25.978
Politically, he represents a red
state Trump won by 40 points.

00:07:25.978 --> 00:07:27.045
But, Sinema, what are you doing?

00:07:27.045 --> 00:07:28.580
Joe Biden won Arizona.

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:30.082
The Cyber Ninjas proved it

00:07:30.082 --> 00:07:34.120
and, if we can't trust
the Cyber Ninjas,

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:36.188
[ Laughter ]
who can we trust?

00:07:36.188 --> 00:07:37.322
I mean, don't tell me

00:07:37.322 --> 00:07:38.623
you're listening
to Rudy Giuliani

00:07:38.623 --> 00:07:40.059
on the Arizona audit.

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:42.028 line:0%
-This chart is almost exactly

00:07:42.028 --> 00:07:44.397 line:0%
the chart that I put out
eight months --

00:07:44.397 --> 00:07:46.331 line:0%
that I gave them
eight months ago.

00:07:46.331 --> 00:07:49.635 line:0%
It has a couple of things,
I mean, a few less.

00:07:49.635 --> 00:07:51.971 line:0%
I mean, we had
about 11,000 dead people

00:07:51.971 --> 00:07:53.472 line:0%
they don't seem to have found.

00:07:53.472 --> 00:07:55.273 line:0%
-Just so you know,
I think dead people;

00:07:55.273 --> 00:07:56.542 line:0%
and I don't think
illegal aliens,

00:07:56.542 --> 00:07:59.478 line:0%
which was your biggest category,
have been gotten to yet.

00:07:59.478 --> 00:08:02.414 line:0%
This is just 50,000
in these categories, 60,000.

00:08:02.414 --> 00:08:05.051 line:0%
-This is not necessarily
about the machines.

00:08:05.051 --> 00:08:07.653 line:0%
This is about what you've always
talked about, Steve.

00:08:07.653 --> 00:08:10.189 line:0%
This is about paper.

00:08:10.189 --> 00:08:11.557 line:0%
This isn't machines.

00:08:11.557 --> 00:08:13.792 line:0%
This is basically --

00:08:13.792 --> 00:08:15.528 line:0%
I mean, what's the
biggest category here?

00:08:15.528 --> 00:08:18.164 line:0%
Mail-in votes
without ballots received.

00:08:18.164 --> 00:08:20.399 line:0%
-[ Laughs ]
-That means phony paper.

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:22.434
-Phony paper, you know,
like your law license.

00:08:22.434 --> 00:08:25.370
I do appreciate that Rudy always
uses visual aids, though.

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:28.007
He's like Carrot Top, but,
instead of protein shakes,

00:08:28.007 --> 00:08:30.943
he lives on a steady diet
of lead paint chips.

00:08:30.943 --> 00:08:33.279
Phony papers is also
what Rudy uses

00:08:33.279 --> 00:08:34.947
when he tries to make
a bank deposit.

00:08:34.947 --> 00:08:37.116
"Sir, um, this is Camel Cash."

00:08:37.116 --> 00:08:39.118
[ As Giuliani ]
Uh, I want to put it
in my savings account.

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:41.020
"Also, this is a blood bank."

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:43.722
Oh, well, in that case,
I need two pints, ASAP.

00:08:43.722 --> 00:08:47.059
[ Laughter ]
Also, why is he making
that face?

00:08:47.059 --> 00:08:49.061
Did he think the camera
was a mirror?

00:08:49.061 --> 00:08:51.997
Was he seeing his teeth
for the first time?

00:08:51.997 --> 00:08:54.233
[ As Giuliani ]
My dental plan
only covers the tops.

00:08:54.233 --> 00:08:56.402
[ Laughter ]

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:58.037
These are the people
who will retake power,

00:08:58.037 --> 00:08:59.605
if Democrats don't get
their [bleep] together

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:01.106
and pass
the transformative agenda

00:09:01.106 --> 00:09:02.508
they promised voters
they would pass,

00:09:02.508 --> 00:09:04.142
because we already know
what it's going to be like

00:09:04.142 --> 00:09:06.712
if Trump or the Trump cultists
in the GOP get back into power.

00:09:06.712 --> 00:09:09.649
In fact, every day, we find out
more about just how insane

00:09:09.649 --> 00:09:11.149
and unhinged
the administration was,

00:09:11.149 --> 00:09:13.552
thanks to the flood of Trump
books that keep coming out.

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:16.354
The latest is from a former
Trump press secretary

00:09:16.354 --> 00:09:17.789
and chief of staff
to Melania Trump

00:09:17.789 --> 00:09:18.857
named Stephanie Grisham.

00:09:18.857 --> 00:09:20.059
Grisham worked

00:09:20.059 --> 00:09:21.794
for this monstrous
administration for years

00:09:21.794 --> 00:09:23.829
and, in the process,
she seems to have collected

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:25.330
some juicy tidbits

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:27.532
for a lucrative book deal,
like this one.

00:09:27.532 --> 00:09:29.267 line:0%
-She writes
that there's

00:09:29.267 --> 00:09:30.903 line:0%
a Trump aide in the White House

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:33.339 line:0%
who was designated
as the Music Man,

00:09:33.339 --> 00:09:35.141 line:0%
to play him
his favorite show tunes,

00:09:35.141 --> 00:09:37.443 line:0%
including "Memory," from "Cats,"

00:09:37.443 --> 00:09:39.145 line:0%
and they would play those songs
-Oh, my God.

00:09:39.145 --> 00:09:41.747 line:0%
-when the president was
in a bit of a rage

00:09:41.747 --> 00:09:44.316 line:0%
and the music was meant
to calm him down.

00:09:44.316 --> 00:09:47.085
-I'm pretty sure that's
the same thing they do at zoos,

00:09:47.085 --> 00:09:49.221
to calm down the gorillas
when they have an erection.

00:09:49.221 --> 00:09:52.124
"Uh-oh, JoJo's looking
aggressive today.

00:09:52.124 --> 00:09:54.393
Someone play
'If I Were a Rich Man.'"

00:09:54.393 --> 00:09:55.527
[ Laughter ]

00:09:55.527 --> 00:09:57.062
Of course,
sometimes the zookeepers

00:09:57.062 --> 00:09:58.731
will accidentally
put on some Barry White

00:09:58.731 --> 00:09:59.965
and that's how you end up
with gorillas

00:09:59.965 --> 00:10:01.834
going down on each other
at The Bronx Zoo.

00:10:01.834 --> 00:10:03.902
[ Laughter ]
Ah, take it down!

00:10:03.902 --> 00:10:05.771
Give them some privacy,
for God's sake.

00:10:05.771 --> 00:10:07.739
That's how graphic it was --
we had to censor it.

00:10:07.739 --> 00:10:10.542
[ New York accent ]
Because it's New York City,
baby!

00:10:10.542 --> 00:10:12.644
Even our zoos gotta be blurred.

00:10:12.644 --> 00:10:15.647
[ Laughter ]
You call your gorilla exhibit...

00:10:15.647 --> 00:10:17.449
We call ours...

00:10:17.449 --> 00:10:20.051
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:10:20.051 --> 00:10:21.486
New York, baby!

00:10:21.486 --> 00:10:24.122
[ Laughter ]
Anyway, back to Trump.

00:10:24.122 --> 00:10:26.091
I bet, when Andrew Lloyd Webber
wrote "Cats,"

00:10:26.091 --> 00:10:27.860
he never thought the soundtrack
would be used

00:10:27.860 --> 00:10:29.595
to save the world
from Armageddon.

00:10:29.595 --> 00:10:31.663
He might be the first composer
to win a Tony

00:10:31.663 --> 00:10:33.665
and a Nobel Peace Prize.

00:10:33.665 --> 00:10:35.935
He could actually EGONT.

00:10:35.935 --> 00:10:38.070
[ Laughter ]
See? This is the kind of thing

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:41.040
we can do in an empty studio.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:43.676
[ Laughter ]

00:10:43.676 --> 00:10:46.011
We're still going to be doing
EGONT jokes

00:10:46.011 --> 00:10:47.379
when the audience comes back.

00:10:47.379 --> 00:10:49.481
[ Laughter ]
Was there a second button,

00:10:49.481 --> 00:10:52.184
next to nuclear button,
